{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrQdA9PA4Ezwc7tMiggQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't open the source, so this diagnosis is inferred from the bug report and the usual layout of this NestJS boilerplate. The retrieved snippets only contain DTOs, Google auth classes and e2e tests. The line numbers are estimates and need checking against the real file.\n\nThe 422 `needLoginViaProvider:google` comes from the provider check in the login flow. That check rejects any user whose stored `provider` isn't `email`. A user who registered by email and was never near Google is being rejected, so their stored `provider` must be wrong. The most likely cause is that registration saves the wrong value. Less likely, the email-confirmation step overwrites it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":12036,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a390b5f2-2370-4dc8-b728-becc01aa43ca","uuid":"bc179f7b-d990-499e-8d4e-32cd0a71bb94","timestamp":"2026-11-09T00:28:52.489Z","request_id":"req_011CgrQd9vVLQ8GvzemRYa24"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrQdA9PA4Ezwc7tMiggQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LpYDRU3XtdY2xq1fiLxB77","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"candidates":[{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.register","start_line":120,"end_line":150,"explanation":"Likely cause (unverified). Registration creates the user through usersService.create(...). If the `provider` it stores isn't `AuthProvidersEnum.email` (for example, it's set to google), the user is saved with the wrong provider. Login then rejects them with `needLoginViaProvider:google`."},{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.validateLogin","start_line":45,"end_line":90,"explanation":"This is where the 422 `needLoginViaProvider:<provider>` is raised, when `user.provider !== AuthProvidersEnum.email`. The check or the error payload may be wrong, for example comparing against the wrong enum value. It only produces the reported message if the stored provider is wrong."},{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.confirmEmail","start_line":190,"end_line":230,"explanation":"Less likely. Confirmation could overwrite the user's `provider` when it updates the status, which would also leave the user with the wrong provider right after confirming."}],"fix":{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","description":"In AuthService.register, create the user with `provider: AuthProvidersEnum.email`. Check that confirmEmail only changes `status` and leaves `provider` alone. Check that validateLogin compares `user.provider` to `AuthProvidersEnum.email`."}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":12036,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"